# Step 28, its third pull request's first part: custom commands, the core's
# guards of an extension's command, a second part. Where a command runs
# nothing (a stop left for the next prompt, a gate held on `prompt.submit`,
# the running turn stopped), where its own stop goes, its time from when it
# is asked, its session values of no turn, whose its question says it is,
# and its `cineris.fs.write`, broken one at a time, with the tests that must
# fail.

[break] a-command-runs-past-a-stop-left-for-the-next-prompt
rule: An extension's command is not run while a stop waits for the next prompt: it is refused with the stop, which it takes.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: run_script
find: hooks.commands.take_stop()
replace: None::<String>
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-command-runs-past-a-held-prompt-gate
rule: An extension's command is not run while a gate on `prompt.submit` is held, which would refuse what it sends.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: run_script
find: hooks.prompt_gate_held()
replace: None::<String>
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-command-runs-while-the-running-turn-is-stopped
rule: An extension's command is not run while the turn running is stopped.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: run_script
find: policy.stopped_for_hooks(running_number)
replace: None::<String>
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-commands-own-stop-is-not-the-sessions
rule: A command's own stop (a question answered with a stop) is told, and refuses the next prompt once, as a hook's stop of no turn does.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/commands.rs
in: run_script
find: hooks.commands.command_stopped(&shown, &note);
replace: let _ = (&shown, &note);
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-commands-time-runs-from-its-start
rule: A command's 30 s run from when it is asked: its wait behind its extension's other call is within them.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/tools.rs
in: LoadedExtension::call_command
find: asked: Some(asked)
replace: asked: Some(asked).filter(|_| false)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-commands-session-value-names-a-turn
rule: A command's `cineris.state` session value is recorded as of no turn.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
in: CallHost::state_set
find: .filter(|_| self.phase != Phase::Command)
replace: .filter(|_| true)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-projects-command-asks-as-yours
rule: What a command of a project's extension asks says it is the project's extension's.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
in: CallHost::asker
in-string: the project's
replace: your
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions

[break] a-users-command-is-not-said-to-be-theirs
rule: What a command of the user's own extension asks says it is theirs.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
in: CallHost::asker
in-string: your
replace: the user's
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::an_interrupt_stops_a_running_command_and_its_questions_are_its_own

[break] a-commands-question-does-not-say-whose
rule: A command's question (`question/ask`) begins with the command and whose it is.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
in: CallHost::ask
in-string: asks: {question}
replace: {question}
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::an_interrupt_stops_a_running_command_and_its_questions_are_its_own

[break] a-commands-approval-does-not-say-whose
rule: A command's approval (`approval/request`'s summary) begins with the command and whose it is.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/host.rs
in: CallHost::decide
in-string: {asker}: {summary}
replace: {summary} ({asker})
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions
    cineris-core::it commands::an_interrupt_stops_a_running_command_and_its_questions_are_its_own

[break] a-command-may-write
rule: `cineris.fs.write` is refused in a command, whatever its manifest lets it write: a command runs outside any round, which would record the change.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/host.rs
in: serve
find: if phase != Phase::Tool {
replace: if phase == Phase::Hook {
packages: cineris-ext, cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it serve::a_hook_cannot_put_a_question_and_only_a_tool_call_writes
    cineris-core::it commands::a_command_runs_nothing_where_its_prompt_would_be_refused_and_its_stop_is_the_sessions
